.UPDATE...
Issued at 918 AM PDT Sat Aug 8 2026

The marine layer was deeper than previously anticipated with the
OAK 12Z upper air sounding showing it around 1,600 feet in depth.
This allowed for widespread stratus to push inland into the
interior valleys this morning, but is now showing signs of
retreating to the coastline. Mid-to-upper level moisture wrapping
around the western periphery of the high pressure over the Four
Corners region is bring mid-to-high level clouds as well. A Heat
Advisory will go into effect at 10 AM this morning and through 10
PM Sunday across much of the interior Bay Area and Central Coast.
Areas under the Heat Advisory will warm into the mid 90s and up to
105 deg F in the warmest interior locations. That said, the
ongoing forecast remains on track at this time with no updates
anticipated at this time.

