.SHORT TERM...
Issued at 1206 AM PDT Sat Aug 8 2026
(Today through Sunday)

Upper-level ridging across the Four Corners will expand westward
Saturday bringing widespread moderate to areas of major HeatRisk to
the interior over the weekend. This will support temperatures 10-15
degrees above normal and a compressed marine layer. While messaging
remains the same, the ridge is forecast to be slower to break down
with northerly/offshore flow developing at 925 mb down the Northern
Sacramento Valley on Sunday. This will make Sunday the hottest of
the two days in some locations, namely the North Bay Interior
Valleys, San Francisco Bayshore, and San Francisco. Have opted to
leave them out of the Heat Advisory still; however, they may need to
be included in subsequent forecasts. Near-critical fire weather
conditions persist through the weekend across the interior due to
very hot and dry conditions. Minor coastal flooding is expected
during the highest high tide (evening/overnight) for bayshore
locations along the San Francisco Bay, San Pablo Bay, and Monterey
Bay through Thursday morning. The Pacific Coast may need to be added
Sunday through Tuesday. Tonight`s forecast was overdone by 0.1 ft
and while that is not a lot, it is the difference of whether or not
the Pacific Coast gets included. We will wait to see how our
forecast performs and what the trend is after Saturday night`s high
tide before we make a decision one way or the other.

