.AVIATION...
(12Z TAFS)
Issued at 505 AM PDT Sat Aug 8 2026

A strong 500 mb high pressure system and large scale compression
continue to slowly decrease the marine layer depth. At the same
time, satellite shows widespread stratus and fog over the coastal
and offshore waters with onshore winds transporting stratus, fog
and mist /MVFR-IFR-LIFR/ inland underneath the high and across low
lying areas of the Bay Area and north Central Coast. Otherwise it
is VFR. In the marine layer temperature inversion across the hills
and mountains it`s much warmer and dry. The SFO-SAC pressure gradient
is 3.0 mb and it is forecast to reach near 4 mb this afternoon.
Stratus and fog have a solid start, however diurnal surface warming
will connect with the lower level temperature inversion and raise the
temperatures and mix out the stratus and fog to the coastline.

Recent high resolution model output has been showing drier northwest
winds arriving later today, tonight and Sunday eroding the coastal
stratus north-south, perhaps leaving a narrow channel of stratus and
fog /IFR-LIFR/ along the immediate coastline along with an inland
intrusion possible tonight and Sunday morning. The high resolution
rapid refresh model leans less stratus and fog and the NAM leans more
stratus and fog remaining; 12-24 hours from now it`s a low confidence
forecast.

Vicinity of SFO...Stratus /IFR/ until 17z today then VFR. Stratus
/IFR/ is forecast 10z Sunday. West to northwest wind 5 to 15 knots
except 15 to 25 knots from late morning through mid evening.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...Stratus, patchy fog and mist /IFR-LIFR/
lifts to MVFR-VFR by late morning. Stratus, patchy fog and mist
/IFR-LIFR/ return tonight and Sunday morning. West to northwest
winds 5 to 15 knots.

