.MARINE...
(Today through Thursday)
Issued at 918 AM PDT Sat Aug 8 2026

Fresh to strong northwest winds continue through the weekend into
the work week with building rough seas up to 12 feet across the
outer coastal waters. The northern coastal waters particularly
will remain hazardous to small craft with occasional near gale
force gusts through the middle of next week. Gusty onshore winds
are forecast through Sunday across the San Francisco Bay north of
the Bay Bridge to the Delta. A long period southerly swell of 15
to 17 seconds prevails through the weekend.

